      text: 'Students tasted chocolate chip cookies from a jar and rated them. Cookies from a jar holding two were liked more than identical cookies from a jar holding ten. They were liked still more when a jar of ten was swapped for a jar of two in front of the taster, and most of all when the experimenter explained that the others had gone to other participants who needed them. Scarcity helped; scarcity because other people wanted the thing helped most.',
