    shadow: 'Triangles are flammable. Jealousy switched on deliberately does not switch off on command, and relationships founded on it tend to stay suspicious and possessive. The third person is often a real human being used as a prop, and they get hurt. People who need rivalry to feel desire learn to want the contest rather than the person, so a partner won by competition may lose interest the moment the competition ends. Mahler’s revived devotion came wrapped in a jealous torment that lasted the rest of his short life.',
