    shadow: 'This is the move closest to abuse. Steadily lowering someone’s self-regard so that they cling to you is the method of coercive control and of cult recruitment, and the pick-up artist’s ‘neg’ is its crudest form. Even when it works, it builds a relationship on manufactured insecurity that has to be kept up, because a person who recovers their confidence has no reason to stay. It also misfires: a target who smells the condescension simply stops liking the seducer.',
    honest: 'Good friends and partners do sometimes show us that we are settling for less. The honest version says so once, kindly, then backs whatever the other person decides, without making itself the only way forward.',
